																		Hello, My name is Elder Ihp, and I would like to share with you this most amazing commentary.
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606661322" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;" >Ihp</a></span> <span class="odate time_1405209898 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Jul 2014 00:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2068225">
									

<p>First and foremost: before people say anything about the Special Containment Procedures being blank: they aren't. I just split them into the Object and Informational Containment Procedures subheadings. The reason I did this is simple: the OCP is meant to say how you keep an object in containment. The ICP<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-230707-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-230707-1')">1</a></sup> is what you say in the event the object somehow leaks from containment. This is especially useful in, say, memetic SCPs. If there's enough outcry about it, I'll take it down and standardize it.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-230707-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-230707-2')">2</a></sup></p>
<p>The original idea I had was based off of a certain actor that's been in movies with names similar to <em>Operation: Implausible</em>, <em>Clash of the Planets</em> and <em>Precipice of the Future</em>. My mother had always said his acting was robotic and stiff, so I decided to make an expy of him that was an actual robot. Then, I got talking to Roget about this idea, and saw that Constellation Starfish for the contest was all about music. So, I got to thinking: what if the robot was powered by music, and it spiraled out from there. This was originally meant to be a character study in the actor himself, but, much like the star of <em>Operation: Implausible</em>, I felt that his personality would be too fake and robotic to work.</p>
<p>Thanks to everyone on chat who looked over this, special thanks to Roget for helping me get this off the ground. Enjoy your silly Fifthist skip.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-230707-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-230707-1')">1</a>. Unfortunate acronym, I know.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-230707-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-230707-2')">2</a>. No I won't.</div>
</div>

