			<div class="content" id="post-content-2160054">
									

<p>I like this article, I think it fits well with pre-existing Fifithsm materials. But I am confused: why does it need to be routinely de-energized? If the object is an android that is powered by (and therefore recharging its battery through) songs of the Constellation Starfish, it should be permanently de-powered once the charge is used up, as long as no songs of the Constellation Starfish are played in its presence.</p>
<p>So why not lock it up in a sound-proof room with no recording equipments, and wait till its power runs out? It will be safe then.</p>
<p>Only explanation I can think of for this issue is that it recharges whenever the Constellation Starfish plays or whenever one of their songs are played anywhere, regardless of geological location of these performances. The problem is then, if the android is recharged every time a song from the Constellation Starfish is played, why does other musical performance of religious intends discharge it only when performed in its presence?</p>
<p>This really bothers me, if that's your intend I believe you should add some information that indicates this is the case; if not, I'd like to know the explanation. Neutral for now.</p>

